<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>True</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Title>Division Compute</Title>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageId>NorthRoc.$(AssemblyName)</PackageId>
    <Version>0.5.0</Version>
    <Authors>Rex Woodfield</Authors>
    <Company>NorthRoc Studios</Company>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <Description>DivisionCompute is a source-to-source compiler and runtime that lets you write HLSL compute shaders directly in C#</Description>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/NorthRocStudios/DivisionCompute</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageTags>compiler;hlsl;shader;translate;compute;gpu;cpu;csharp;windows</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Added:
- Build-time shader generation: a Roslyn source generator translates [Shader] structs during dotnet build and bakes HLSL, kernel names, resource layout, packed uniform layout, and a normalized source hash into the assembly (no Roslyn or reflection at startup)
- Hot reload detection: if a shader's source file changes after the build, TranslateShader falls back to Roslyn automatically and CreateShader uses reflection layouts (UsedGeneratedDescriptor=false); disable with DIVISION_DISABLE_SOURCE_CHANGE_DETECTION=1
- Runtime translation is still the fallback: PreferGeneratedDescriptors, DIVISION_FORCE_RUNTIME_TRANSLATION=1, [Shader(GenerateDescriptor = false)], and DivisionShaderDescriptors.Unregister
- Shader translation errors now surface as build errors (DIVSGEN001/DIVSGEN002)
- TranslateShaders / CompileShaders batch APIs that parallelize across shaders and share one Roslyn compilation
- Kernel compilation (D3DCompile) now runs in parallel across a shader's kernels
- Structured-buffer element structs declared in referenced assemblies are emitted from metadata
- Symbol-based uniform/resource layout shared by the runtime translator and the generator
Changed:
- One Roslyn compilation and metadata reference set per project instead of one per shader (~20x cheaper per translation); UseSharedCompilation=false restores the old behaviour
- Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp replaces the Microsoft.CodeAnalysis meta-package (smaller deployment)
Fixed:
- Structured-buffer element validation now applies when translating from source without a runtime type
- Cross-file struct declarations are translated with the semantic model of their own syntax tree</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Rex Woodfield and NorthRoc Studios contributors</Copyright>
    <RootNamespace>DivisionEngine</RootNamespace>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp" Version="5.12.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="NorthRoc.DivisionMath" Version="0.3.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Vortice.D3DCompiler" Version="3.8.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Vortice.Direct3D11" Version="3.8.3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The source generator translates [Shader] structs at build time. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DivisionCompute.SourceGenerators\DivisionCompute.SourceGenerators.csproj" OutputItemType="Analyzer" ReferenceOutputAssembly="false" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Ship the generator inside the package so consumers get build-time shaders just by
    referencing NorthRoc.DivisionCompute. NuGet treats any DLL under
    analyzers/dotnet/cs as a Roslyn analyzer.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage>$(TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage);PackDivisionShaderGenerator</TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="PackDivisionShaderGenerator">
    <ItemGroup>
      <TfmSpecificPackageFile Include="$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\..\DivisionCompute.SourceGenerators\bin\$(Configuration)\net10.0\DivisionCompute.SourceGenerators.dll">
        <PackagePath>analyzers/dotnet/cs</PackagePath>
      </TfmSpecificPackageFile>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
